---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Rosette from '../components/Rosette.astro';
import '../styles/prose.css';
---

<Base title="About" description="A little about Nils, and where the name nil.ski comes from.">
  <section class="measure intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Hi, I'm <span class="mark">Nils</span>.</h1>
  </section>

  <div class="measure prose">
    <p>
      Placeholder copy — swap it for a few lines about who you are, what you do and what you'd like
      people to get in touch about.
    </p>

    <h2 id="the-name">Why nil.ski?</h2>

    <div class="name-card" aria-label="Nils plus -ski makes Nilski">
      <span>Nils</span>
      <span class="op">+</span>
      <span class="suffix">-ski</span>
      <span class="op">=</span>
      <span class="result">Nil<em>ski</em></span>
    </div>

    <p>
      My mum is Polish; her surname is Kotowska. I grew up with a Swedish surname instead, but had I
      carried hers, it would have been <strong>Kotowski</strong>. Polish surnames like this change their ending:
      <em>-ska</em> for women, <em>-ski</em> for men.
    </p>
    <p>
      So nil.ski is my name, given the Polish ending I never had: <strong>Nils</strong> + <strong>-ski</strong>.
      The paper-cut rosettes around the site are a nod to <em>wycinanki</em>, the colourful Polish folk-art
      cutouts.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site used to live at <a href="https://misiu.co">misiu.co</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="about-rosette"><Rosette size="7rem" /></div>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 5rem) 1.5rem;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-variation-settings: 'SOFT' 100, 'WONK' 1, 'opsz' 144;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
  }

  .name-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.35em 0.6em;
    padding: 1.4rem 1rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, #fff 55%, transparent);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 4.5vw, 2rem);
    font-variation-settings: 'SOFT' 100, 'WONK' 1;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .op {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: 0.7em;
  }

  .suffix {
    color: var(--coral);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .result em {
    color: var(--coral);
  }

  .about-rosette {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 4rem;
  }
</style>
